===Prepositional phrase===
{{en-prep phrase|[[at]] [[arm's length]]}}

# At a [[distance]], away from one's body.
#* {{quote-journal|en|work=BBC Sport|author=Phil McNulty|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/53955829|date=5 September 2020|title=Iceland 0-1 England|passage=Iceland were defiant, as they always are, rigid in defence and lacking in attacking ambition, willing to simply keep England '''at arm's length''' and maybe land a counter-punch.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} Avoiding a close [[relationship]].
#: ''She's been keeping me '''at arm's length''' all the time. She doesn't want to get involved.''

